################## वाक्सञ्चयः ~ संस्कृत-वाणी-कोशः ##################
#### Vāksañcayaḥ ~ Saṃskṛtam Speech Corpus by IIT Bombay ####

About
=============================================================
Vāksañcayaḥ - Sanskrit speech corpus has more than 78 hours of data and contains recordings of 45,953 sentences with a sampling rate of 22 KHz. The content is mainly readings of various texts spanning many Śāstras of Saṃskṛt literature and also includes contemporary stories, radio program, extempore discourse, etc.

Citing the corpus
=============================================================
If you use this corpus or its derivate resources for your research, kindly cite it as follows:
Devaraja Adiga, Rishabh Kumar, Amrith Krishna, Preethi Jyothi, Ganesh Ramakrishnan, and Pawan Goyal. "Automatic Speech Recognition in Sanskrit: A New Speech Corpus and Modelling Insights". Proceedings of The 59th Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics (ACL Findings), 2021.
Paper Link : https://arxiv.org/abs/2106.05852

Pre-processing
=============================================================
Audio files which are in the MP3 format can be converted to the WAV format using the script (mp3_to_wav.sh) provided along with the corpus for training ASR systems. This script requires unix platform to run. To run the script, "sox" package needs to be installed. If it is not installed use the command "sudo apt install sox" and run it in the terminal. Then run ./mp3_to_wav.sh from the terminal.

