Transcript Details
=============================================================
1. Anusvāra at the word ending is represented as "म्" for the simplicity.
2. Anusvāra before क्, ख्, ग, घ्, ङ् are replaced by ङ् and similarly when the Anusvāra is followed by other four set of row consonants, corresponding 5th nasal consonant is used for replacing that Anusvāra.
3. Transcripts are given both in Devanagari and SLP1. Each text file gives the transcirption for that particular speaker.
4. Transcripts has an unique id (corresponds to the audio file) followed by text.
5. Transcripts id begins with a speaker identifier, followed by  audio file number for that particular speaker and original audio identifier. 

Speaker Details
=============================================================
Below are the list of speaker ids used in the experimental results reported in our ACL-2021 paper:
Training : sp001, sp002, sp003, sp004, sp006, sp008, sp009, sp012, sp016, sp019, sp020, sp021
Validation : sp005, sp013, sp014, sp017
Test : sp007, sp010, sp011, sp015, sp018, sp022
Out-of-Domain-Test : sp023, sp024, sp025, sp026, sp027 (Description of Out-of-Domain-Test dataset is given in the paper)
